        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Piney%2C_Wyoming"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was named after Big Piney Creek, which took its name from the pine trees growing along the banks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Piney%2C_Wyoming"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Big Piney was once called the Ice Box of the Nation after becoming an official weather station in 1930.",
